/******************************************************************************
    # VOTIX BUTTON
 *******************************************************************************/

/*
## Overview

`VotixButton` is a versatile button component that adapts to your app's theme,
offering multiple variants, sizes, and states. It automatically handles
light/dark mode switching and provides consistent styling throughout your app.
*/

/*
## Features

- Multiple variants: primary, secondary, outline, text, gradient
- Size options: small, medium, large
- Loading state with spinner animation
- Icons: supports leading and trailing icons
- Adaptive theming: automatically handles light/dark mode
- Flexible width: wraps content, fixed width, or full width
- Custom gradients for gradient variant
*/

/*
## Usage Examples

```dart
// Basic primary button
VotixButton(
  text: 'Submit',
  onPressed: handleSubmit,
)

// Secondary button with icon
VotixButton(
  text: 'Add to Cart',
  onPressed: addToCart,
  variant: VotixButtonVariant.secondary,
  leadingIcon: Icons.shopping_cart,
)

// Outline button
VotixButton(
  text: 'Cancel',
  onPressed: handleCancel,
  variant: VotixButtonVariant.outline,
)

// Loading state
VotixButton(
  text: 'Loading Example',
  onPressed: handlePress,
  isLoading: isLoading, // Set to true to show spinner
)

// Full width gradient button
VotixButton(
  text: 'Create Account',
  onPressed: createAccount,
  variant: VotixButtonVariant.gradient,
  width: double.infinity,
)
```
*/

/*
## Button Variants

### Primary (Default)
The standard button with solid background in your primary brand color.
Best for primary actions like "Submit", "Save", or "Continue".

### Secondary
Uses mint/secondary colors instead of primary colors.
Good for secondary actions or to create visual hierarchy.

### Outline
Transparent background with colored border.
Useful for less prominent actions or in dense UIs.

### Text
No background or border, just text and optional icon.
Ideal for low-emphasis actions or tight spaces.

### Gradient
Uses beautiful gradients from your app theme.
Best for main call-to-action buttons or featured actions.
*/

/*
## Button Sizes

### Small (36px height)
For tight spaces or secondary actions.

### Medium (48px height)
Standard size for most buttons.

### Large (56px height)
For primary call-to-action buttons.
*/

/*
## Properties

| Property | Type | Default | Description |
|----------|------|---------|-------------|
| text | String | required | Text to display on the button |
| onPressed | VoidCallback? | required | Callback when button is pressed |
| variant | VotixButtonVariant | primary | Visual style of the button |
| size | VotixButtonSize | medium | Size of the button |
| leadingIcon | IconData? | null | Optional icon to show before text |
| trailingIcon | IconData? | null | Optional icon to show after text |
| isLoading | bool | false | Whether to show a loading indicator |
| iconSize | double? | null | Optional icon size override |
| width | double? | null | Optional width to make button fill available space |
| customGradient | LinearGradient? | null | Optional custom gradient for gradient variant |
| borderRadius | double? | null | Optional rounded corners radius |
| elevation | double? | null | Optional elevation for the button |
*/

/*
## Implementation Details

The button component uses your existing color system from `VotixColors` and
adapts to the current theme automatically. It implements multiple builders for
different variants to maintain a consistent look and feel while providing
distinct visual styles.

The architecture follows a modular approach, where base styles are extended
with variant-specific modifications.
*/

/******************************************************************************
    # VOTIX TEXT FIELD
 *******************************************************************************/

/*
## Overview

`VotixTextField` is a professionally styled text input component that adapts to
your app's theme, offering multiple variants, input types, and states. It
provides built-in validation, formatting, and error handling.
*/

/*
## Features

- Multiple variants: outlined, filled, underlined, minimal
- Smart input types with built-in validation: text, email, password, phone, etc.
- Automatic light/dark mode adaptation
- Error states and validation
- Helper text and hint support
- Prefix/suffix icons and widgets
- Character counter
- Multi-line support
*/

/*
## Usage Examples

```dart
// Basic text field
VotixTextField(
  label: 'Username',
  hint: 'Enter your username',
)

// Email input with validation
VotixTextField(
  label: 'Email',
  hint: 'Enter your email',
  inputType: VotixInputType.email,
  required: true,
)

// Password input with toggle visibility
VotixTextField(
  label: 'Password',
  hint: 'Enter your password',
  inputType: VotixInputType.password,
  required: true,
)

// Search field
VotixTextField(
  hint: 'Search...',
  inputType: VotixInputType.search,
  prefixIcon: Icons.search,
  variant: VotixInputVariant.filled,
  borderRadius: 24,
)

// Multi-line input
VotixTextField(
  label: 'Message',
  hint: 'Enter your message',
  inputType: VotixInputType.multiline,
  minLines: 3,
  maxLines: 5,
)
```
*/

/*
## Input Variants

### Outlined (Default)
Standard input with a visible border.
Best for forms and data entry.

### Filled
Input with a filled background.
Good for search fields and contexts where you want to visually distinguish inputs.

### Underlined
Minimalist input with only a bottom line.
Creates a cleaner look in some UIs.

### Minimal
Ultra-clean input with no borders, just hint/label.
For very clean, minimal interfaces.
*/

/*
## Input Types

### Text
Standard text input with no special validation.

### Email
Email input with email validation and appropriate keyboard.

### Password
Password input with toggle to show/hide and security features.

### Phone
Phone number input with formatting and appropriate keyboard.

### Number
Numeric input that only accepts digits.

### Multiline
For paragraphs and longer content.

### Search
Optimized for search functionality.

### URL
Web address with validation and appropriate keyboard.
*/

/*
## Properties

| Property | Type | Default | Description |
|----------|------|---------|-------------|
| controller | TextEditingController? | null | Controller for the text input |
| label | String? | null | Label text shown above or within the input |
| hint | String? | null | Hint text shown when the input is empty |
| helperText | String? | null | Helper text shown below the input |
| errorText | String? | null | Error text shown below the input |
| prefixIcon | IconData? | null | Icon to show at the start of the input |
| suffixIcon | IconData? | null | Icon to show at the end of the input |
| prefix | Widget? | null | Custom widget to show at the start of the input |
| suffix | Widget? | null | Custom widget to show at the end of the input |
| variant | VotixInputVariant | outlined | Visual style of the input |
| inputType | VotixInputType | text | Type of input with built-in validation |
| enabled | bool | true | Whether the input is enabled |
| required | bool | false | Whether the input is required |
| autofocus | bool | false | Whether the input should have focus when first displayed |
| onChanged | Function(String)? | null | Callback when text changes |
| onSubmitted | Function(String)? | null | Callback when form is submitted |
| validator | String? Function(String?)? | null | Validator function for form validation |
| focusNode | FocusNode? | null | Focus node for controlling focus |
| onTap | VoidCallback? | null | Callback when field is tapped |
| maxLength | int? | null | Maximum number of characters allowed |
| maxLines | int? | null | Maximum number of lines for multiline input |
| minLines | int? | null | Minimum number of lines for multiline input |
| capitalization | TextCapitalization | none | Text capitalization style |
| inputFormatters | List<TextInputFormatter>? | null | Input formatters for text formatting |
| textInputAction | TextInputAction? | null | Text input action (e.g., next, done, search) |
| borderRadius | double? | null | Custom border radius |
| showCounter | bool | false | Whether to show counter for character count |
| backgroundColor | Color? | null | Optional custom background color |
| borderColor | Color? | null | Optional custom border color |
| textColor | Color? | null | Optional custom text color |
| contentPadding | EdgeInsetsGeometry? | null | Content padding |
*/

/*
## Implementation Details

The TextField component uses your existing theme system and color palette,
ensuring consistent styling. It automatically configures itself with the right
keyboard type, validation rules, and special features based on the input type.

For password fields, it provides a visibility toggle icon.
For required fields, it provides built-in validation.
*/

/******************************************************************************
    # VOTIX TEXT
 *******************************************************************************/

/*
## Overview

`VotixText` is a versatile typography component that standardizes text styling
throughout your app. It supports all Material 3 typography styles, multiple
emphasis levels, and special text treatments like gradients.
*/

/*
## Features

- Complete typography system (15 text styles from Material 3)
- Multiple emphasis levels (high, medium, low, brand, etc.)
- Text treatments: bold, italic, underline, strikethrough
- Gradient text support
- Automatic dark/light mode adaptation
- Overflow handling: ellipsis, fade, clip, or auto-sizing
- Selectable text option for copy/paste
*/

/*
## Usage Examples

```dart
// Basic text with default style (bodyMedium)
VotixText('Hello World')

// Display text with brand color
VotixText(
  'Welcome to Votix',
  style: VotixTextStyle.displayLarge,
  emphasis: VotixTextEmphasis.brand,
)

// Body text with multiple lines
VotixText(
  'This is a paragraph of text that can span multiple lines.',
  style: VotixTextStyle.bodyMedium,
  maxLines: 3,
)

// Error message
VotixText.error(
  'Please check your network connection',
  isBold: true,
)

// Gradient text
VotixText.gradient(
  'Featured Content',
  style: VotixTextStyle.headlineMedium,
)

// Named constructors for common patterns
VotixText.headline('Section Title')
VotixText.body('Paragraph text goes here...')
VotixText.label('Form Label')
```
*/

/*
## Text Styles

### Display (Large, Medium, Small)
For the largest headings and titles.
- displayLarge: 57px
- displayMedium: 45px
- displaySmall: 36px

### Headline (Large, Medium, Small)
For section headers.
- headlineLarge: 32px
- headlineMedium: 28px
- headlineSmall: 24px

### Title (Large, Medium, Small)
For subsection headers and important text.
- titleLarge: 22px
- titleMedium: 16px
- titleSmall: 14px

### Body (Large, Medium, Small)
For main content text.
- bodyLarge: 16px
- bodyMedium: 14px
- bodySmall: 12px

### Label (Large, Medium, Small)
For captions, form labels, and auxiliary text.
- labelLarge: 14px
- labelMedium: 12px
- labelSmall: 11px
*/

/*
## Emphasis Levels

### High
Primary text with maximum readability.

### Medium
Secondary text for supporting information.

### Low
Tertiary text with minimum visual impact.

### Brand
Uses your primary brand color (purple).

### Secondary
Uses your secondary brand color (mint).

### Error
For error messages.

### Success
For success messages.

### Inverted
Automatically inverts based on theme (white on dark, dark on light).
*/

/*
## Named Constructors

### VotixText.display()
For largest headings.

### VotixText.headline()
For section headers.

### VotixText.title()
For component titles.

### VotixText.body()
For main content.

### VotixText.label()
For form labels and captions.

### VotixText.gradient()
For gradient-filled text.

### VotixText.error()
For error messages.

### VotixText.success()
For success messages.
*/

/*
## Properties

| Property | Type | Default | Description |
|----------|------|---------|-------------|
| text | String | required | The text to display |
| style | VotixTextStyle | bodyMedium | The typography style variant |
| emphasis | VotixTextEmphasis | high | The emphasis level affecting color |
| color | Color? | null | Optional custom color (overrides emphasis) |
| decoration | VotixTextDecoration | none | Text decoration type |
| isBold | bool | false | Whether to make text bold |
| isItalic | bool | false | Whether to make text italic |
| isFilled | bool | false | Whether to use a gradient fill |
| gradient | Gradient? | null | Custom gradient for gradient decoration |
| maxLines | int? | null | Maximum number of lines before truncating |
| overflow | TextOverflow | ellipsis | How to handle overflow |
| textAlign | TextAlign | start | Text alignment |
| isSoftened | bool | false | Whether to soften text (reduce opacity) |
| textScaleFactor | double | 1.0 | Scale factor for the text |
| letterSpacing | double? | null | Letter spacing adjustment |
| lineHeight | double? | null | Line height multiplier |
| autoSize | bool | false | Whether text should automatically adjust its font size |
| minFontSize | double? | null | Minimum text size for autoSize |
| selectable | bool | false | Whether to selectable (for copy/paste) |
| semanticLabel | String? | null | Optional semantic label for accessibility |
*/

/*
## Implementation Details

The Text component reads from your existing theme system and color palette to
ensure consistent typography. It follows a "base + modifiers" pattern, where
the base style comes from your theme, and various modifiers (emphasis, weight,
decoration) are applied on top.

For gradient text, it uses a ShaderMask to create the gradient effect while
maintaining the text's inherent properties.
*/

/******************************************************************************
    # VOTIX SIZE
 *******************************************************************************/

/*
## Overview

`VotixSize` is a comprehensive sizing system that standardizes dimensions and
spacing throughout your app. It provides consistent spacing, border radius,
icon sizes, and responsive design utilities.
*/

/*
## Features

- Standardized spacing system based on 4-point grid
- Border radius standards for consistent rounded corners
- Icon size standards for consistent iconography
- Component size standards (buttons, inputs, avatars, etc.)
- Responsive design utilities and breakpoints
- Helper extension methods for cleaner code
*/

/*
## Usage Examples

```dart
// Spacing between elements
VotixSize.m.vertical, // Creates a SizedBox with height

// Padding for containers
Container(
  padding: VotixSize.padding,
  child: Text('Hello'),
)

// With extension methods
Text('Hello').withPadding()
Text('Hello').paddingH() // Horizontal padding only

// Border radius
Container(
  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    borderRadius: VotixSize.borderRadius.rounded,
  ),
)

// Responsive sizing
Text(
  'Responsive Heading',
  style: TextStyle(
    fontSize: VotixSize.responsive(
      context,
      mobile: 18,
      tablet: 24,
      desktop: 32,
    ),
  ),
)

// Grid system
GridView.builder(
  gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: VotixSize.getGridColumnCount(context),
    crossAxisSpacing: VotixSize.r,
    mainAxisSpacing: VotixSize.r,
  ),
)
```
*/

/*
## Spacing System

### Size Constants
- xs: 4px (Micro spacing for tight areas)
- s: 8px (Small spacing for related elements)
- m: 12px (Medium spacing for most elements)
- r: 16px (Regular spacing for container padding)
- l: 24px (Large spacing for separation between sections)
- xl: 32px (Extra large spacing for major section breaks)
- xxl: 48px (Double extra large spacing for very significant separations)
- xxxl: 64px (Triple extra large spacing, maximum standard spacing)

### Common Paddings
- padding: EdgeInsets.all(r) (Standard padding for content containers)
- paddingH: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: r) (Horizontal-only padding)
- paddingV: EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: r) (Vertical-only padding)
- paddingSmall: EdgeInsets.all(s) (Smaller padding for tight containers)
- paddingLarge: EdgeInsets.all(l) (Larger padding for prominent containers)
*/

/*
## Border Radius

- borderRadiusSmall: 4px (For subtle rounding)
- borderRadiusMedium: 8px (Default radius for most elements)
- borderRadius: 12px (Standard radius for cards, buttons)
- borderRadiusLarge: 16px (For more prominent rounding)
- borderRadiusXL: 24px (Maximum standard radius)
- borderRadiusCircular: 50px (For circular elements)
*/

/*
## Icon Sizes

- iconSizeTiny: 12px (For very small contexts)
- iconSizeSmall: 16px (For compact UIs)
- iconSize: 20px (Default size for most icons)
- iconSizeLarge: 24px (For more prominent icons)
- iconSizeXL: 32px (For featured icons)
- iconSizeXXL: 48px (For major focal points)
*/

/*
## Breakpoints

- breakpointMobile: 600px
- breakpointTablet: 905px
- breakpointDesktop: 1240px
- breakpointLargeDesktop: 1440px
*/

/*
## Helper Methods

### Responsive Sizing
- responsive() - Returns size based on screen width
- responsivePadding() - Returns horizontal padding based on screen size
- percentOfWidth() - Calculates percentage of screen width
- percentOfHeight() - Calculates percentage of screen height

### Widget Extensions
- withPadding() - Add padding to a widget
- withMargin() - Add margin to a widget
- paddingH() - Add symmetric horizontal padding
- paddingV() - Add symmetric vertical padding
- paddingAll() - Add all-sides padding with a custom value
- constrained() - Constrain the widget with responsive constraints
- responsiveBox() - Center the widget and apply responsive constraints

### Double Extensions
- insets - Convert to EdgeInsets with all equal sides
- insetsH - Convert to horizontal symmetric EdgeInsets
- insetsV - Convert to vertical symmetric EdgeInsets
- rounded - Convert to BorderRadius with all equal corners
- box - Create a SizedBox with equal width and height
- horizontal - Create a SizedBox with this width and zero height
- vertical - Create a SizedBox with this height and zero width
*/

/*
## Implementation Details

The sizing system is implemented as a utility class with static constants and
methods. It uses extension methods to provide a cleaner API for common
operations. All values are based on a 4-point grid system to ensure consistent
visual rhythm throughout the app.

The responsive utilities automatically detect the device size and adjust
values accordingly, ensuring your UI looks great on all screen sizes.
*/

/*
# Integration Guide

These components work together as a cohesive design system:

1. VotixSize provides the foundation with consistent spacing and dimensions
2. VotixText builds on top of this with standardized typography
3. VotixTextField and VotixButton use both sizing and typography standards

All components automatically adapt to light and dark themes by leveraging your
existing VotixColors and VotixTheme classes.

## Best Practices

- Use VotixSize constants for all dimensions to maintain consistency
- Leverage VotixText for all text to ensure typographic harmony
- Use extension methods for cleaner, more readable code
- Let components automatically adapt to the current theme
*/
